# External systems (default read-only)

- **Writable:** workspace root only (local edits; local commits with no remote effect).
- **Read-only by default:** network services, remote git, MCP/API, paths outside workspace.

| Action | Default |
|--------|---------|
| Read, search, list, fetch, download, clone for study | **Allow** |
| Create, update, delete, publish, comment, upload, or otherwise mutate external state | **Deny** |

User must **name** the write (push, PR, Jira ticket, Slack message, etc.) or a session user rule must require it. Task phrasing alone is not permission.

When a domain has its own rule, follow it for allow/deny detail.

| Domain | Rule |
|--------|------|
| GitHub and Git remotes | [github-and-remotes.mdc](github-and-remotes.mdc) |

No domain rule yet → ask before writing. No stricter `AGENTS.md` or project rule may be overridden.
